data
  title What goes in a metric label?
  desc The cardinality question every new label must answer
  compares
    - label Bounded value → safe as a label
      children
        - label Small fixed set
          desc route templates (20), status_class (4), customer_segment (3)
        - label 20 × 5 × 4 = 400 series
          desc multiplicative, but stays small
        - label Fits the safe zone
          desc ~5M series budget on a 16 GB box
        - label Queryable for years
          desc pre-aggregated at the source
    - label Unbounded value → keep out of labels
      children
        - label High-cardinality identifier
          desc user_id (100k), customer_email
        - label 20 × 5 × 4 × 100k = 40M series
          desc 3 KB each → ~120 GB → OOM
        - label Route it elsewhere
          desc logs (free cardinality) or traces (sampled)
        - label Pivot via exemplar
          desc trace_id on a histogram bucket, no series cost
